<%# Discover / search screen (Hoojah 2026 redesign Phase 2.4) — mockup ~881-935
    "Discover · search & hashtags". Three parts:

      1. `shared/navbar` + `hujahs/feed_tabs` (existing chrome — Discover is already
         the third feed tab; unchanged by this task).
      2. The search bar: a plain GET <form> to `search_path`, deliberately OUTSIDE the
         results turbo-frame and carrying `data-turbo-frame: "search-results"` so a
         submit — native (JS off: a full page reload, this same template, same frame
         id lands in the same place) or Stimulus-driven (JS on:
         `search_controller.js`'s debounced `requestSubmit()`) — always resolves to
         the SAME frame-swap. Keeping the <input> outside the frame means a
         live-suggest swap never yanks focus out of it mid-keystroke.
      3. `search/_results` — the turbo-frame body. `SearchController#index` re-renders
         it on every GET (full page, JS-off submit, or live-suggest fetch alike), so
         there is exactly one server-side branch for "what results look like". %>
<%= render "shared/navbar" %>

<main class="max-w-xl mx-auto px-4 py-6">
  <%= render "hujahs/feed_tabs" %>

  <h1 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink tracking-tight mt-2">Discover</h1>

  <%= form_with url: search_path, method: :get,
        data: {controller: "search", turbo_frame: "search-results"}, class: "mt-3" do %>
    <div class="flex items-center gap-2.5 h-[46px] px-3.5 rounded-xl bg-card-2 border-[1.5px] border-transparent focus-within:border-primary">
      <%= lucide_icon "search", class: "w-[18px] h-[18px] text-primary shrink-0" %>
      <%= text_field_tag :q, @query, placeholder: "Search Hoojah", autocomplete: "off",
            "aria-label": "Search", data: {action: "input->search#queryChanged"},
            class: "flex-1 min-w-0 bg-transparent border-0 focus:ring-0 focus:outline-none p-0 text-sm font-semibold text-ink placeholder:text-ink-2 placeholder:font-normal" %>
    </div>
    <%# Explicit submit control — a lone text input's implicit Enter-to-submit is not
        guaranteed across assistive tech, and it is what makes the JS-off path
        exercisable at all under Capybara's rack_test driver, which has no keyboard
        events. `sr-only`: the magnifier glyph already reads as "search" visually. %>
    <button type="submit" class="sr-only">Search</button>
  <% end %>

  <turbo-frame id="search-results" class="block mt-4">
    <%= render "search/results" %>
  </turbo-frame>
</main>
